Participation Windows
A Participation Window is an open invitation connected to a question, responsibility field, Expedition, tool, prototype or unresolved problem.
Instead of waiting until a project is complete, Spiral Civilization may make its unfinished architecture visible.
A Participation Window may show:

what is currently being investigated
what already exists
what remains unknown
what knowledge or expertise is needed
what proposals already exist
what perspectives are missing
what needs to be researched, tested or built
how a person, institution or AI may contribute
what the next stage of development could be
Participation may take the form of a criterion, critique, research source, experiment, precedent, model, scenario, technical solution, artistic interpretation, or an entirely different approach.
An unfinished structure is not necessarily a weakness.
It can become an invitation to improve it.
