Public and Private Participation
Participation should not require public visibility.
The developing system is intended to distinguish between information used for cooperation and information a participant chooses to make public.
A participant may eventually be able to choose between different levels of visibility, including:
Private participation — information is used only for direct project cooperation.
Public participation — selected information may appear in the public Cooperation Network.
Anonymous contribution — a contribution may become part of the research without publicly identifying its author, where appropriate.
Submission does not automatically create a public profile.
Information should not be displayed publicly without the participant's consent.
The participant should remain able to determine which parts of their participation are intended for public presentation.
